  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\n\nTuesday will see the deformation zone of the sfc low wrap back \naround into the area, resulting in more rain showers and storms. \nStrong cold advection and subsidence behind the low should drive \nsome of the strong H8 winds downward resulting in gusty 40 to 45 mph \nsfc winds. The windy conditions taper off late Tuesday evening from \nwest to east.\n\nThe mid-level wave and any lingering precip across our far north \nfinally departs Wednesday afternoon, although model guidance does \nshow some differences in how fast the wave ejects east. Models hint \nat another compact, weakening H5 shortwave that ejects from the \nRockies area toward the Central Plains Thursday. The track of the \nwave will largely play a role on if we'll see additional rain \nchances that day: NBM is currently dry for the area. More rain \nchances arrive by the weekend, but significant model\ndiscrepancies regarding placement of features are seen at this \npoint. \n\nTemperatures largely remain in the 50s and 60s Tuesday through \nSaturday with the coolest conditions expected across our far \nnorthern areas.",
